[center][size=6][b]ER Echo[/b][/size]
[size=4]Summon characters from your own save files as companions.[/size][/center]

[line]

[center][b][color=#ff6b6b]OFFLINE ONLY.[/color][/b] Use Mod Engine 2 and launch the game without Easy Anti-Cheat.
Never take a modded save online — that is a soft-ban. Back up your save first.[/center]

[line]

[b][size=4]What this is[/size][/b]

ER Echo turns a Spirit Ash into [b]a character taken from one of your own save slots[/b]: same face, same
armour and weapons, same level, same memorised spells. The clone fights with the game's [b]native enemy AI[/b]
(no scripted follow, no puppeteering), follows you like a Spirit Ash, and is summoned the same way — sit at a
Site of Grace, use an Ash, or press a hotkey.

It is a DLL mod for [b]ELDEN RING 1.17.2[/b] and runs under Mod Engine 2 or me3 (vanilla install or Convergence).
It does not edit your save file. The only game data it ships is one patched copy of the vanilla talk ESD
(mod\script\talk), which the grace-menu patch needs, plus two JSON parameter-ID tables derived from the
Convergence regulation (the exporter uses them to validate item IDs). (The optional "root menu fallback" file
is a different ESD variant - only use it if the default menu entry fails to appear.)

A one-click installer ([b]ER-Echo-Setup.exe[/b]) does the setup, the character export and the loader config;
nothing else needs to be edited by hand. A built-in companion ([b]Sanvenir[/b], Lv1) is included, so the mod is
playable before you export anything.

[b][size=4]Features[/size][/b]

[list]
[*][b]Your other Tarnished, not a generic NPC.[/b] Export a character from any save slot (including old,
   "retired" saves) and the clone gets its exact appearance, body shape, 22 equipment slots, level, stats and
   spells.
[*][b]Works before you export anything.[/b] A built-in Lv1 companion (**Sanvenir**) ships with the mod and is
   pinned at the end of the profile list, so a fresh machine still has someone to summon.
[*][b]Up to 3 companions at once[/b], each from a different profile, switchable in-game.
[*][b]Native behaviour.[/b] Clones use the game's own AI think/behaviour params. They detect enemies, engage,
   guard, cast, and follow through the same systems a Spirit Ash uses — including the ash's own catch-up
   teleport when they fall behind.
[*][b]No area restrictions.[/b] F8 and auto-summon work anywhere: no Summoning Pool, no "you can't summon
   here" dead zone, no one-party-at-a-time limit. (Using the Spirit Ash [i]item[/i] itself still follows the
   vanilla dead-zone rule - the item is checked by the game's own menu code.)
[*][b]Sites of Grace menu.[/b] A new entry at the top of the grace menu opens a nested sub-menu: party size
   (0–3), slot assignment, per-companion AI, resummon, friendly fire, back. Injected into the live menu at
   runtime; the archive includes the talk ESD it needs (mounted through mod_loader).
[*][b]Per-companion AI.[/b] Give each of the three slots its own style — Default / Balanced / Melee / Caster /
   Guardian / Aggressive. The choice is saved into that companion's profile JSON, so it follows the character
   across sessions. Spell count applies immediately; engage range / guard / target switching apply on the next
   summon. Profiles with no AI setting keep following the global weights.
[*][b]Player-level damage.[/b] Companions use the Tarnished's damage correction: the vanilla Spirit Ash debuff
   (damage ×0.25, damage taken ×0.5, poise ×0.05) and the extra poise-taken modifier are removed from the clone
   only, so other Spirit Ashes keep their vanilla numbers.
[*][b]Level-ups carry over.[/b] When you level up at a Site of Grace, every loaded companion follows with the same
   stat gains, gets its live level/stats/HP-FP-stamina updated, and the new values are written back to its
   profile JSON.
[*][b]Optional friendly fire.[/b] The menu can enable player ↔ companion hits at 20% damage
   (configurable). Companions keep their buddy AI (they never treat you as an enemy) and cannot be
   locked on, so you won't accidentally snap the camera to them. Damage to ordinary enemies is unchanged.
[*][b]Comrade-mode enemy HP correction.[/b] Enemy max HP scales with the number of [b]living[/b] companions:
   1 / 2 / 3 → ×1.5 / ×1.8 / ×2.0 (×1.0 with none). Bosses already in combat scale immediately and keep
   their current HP percentage. Implemented at runtime; [i]NpcParam[/i] / [i]regulation.bin[/i] are untouched.
   Configurable in [i]er_echo.ini[/i] (the balance section) and diagnosable with [i]enemy_hp_status[/i].
[*][b]Auto-summon[/b] after resting, fast travel or resurrection (optional).
[*][b]Give gear to a companion[/b] — press [b]F12[/b] on an item in your inventory/equipment menu and the
   selected companion receives it. With no equipment item selected, [b]F12[/b] restores that companion's
   profile loadout (equipment and spells) instead of copying yours.
[*][b]Optional LLM "battle director"[/b] (Python sidecar, off by default). It reads combat state and nudges
   aggression / spell rate / guard rate / target switching. The LLM can also swap a clone's gear or stats, with
   whitelists, clamps and a rollback point. It only ever touches the clones — never your character.
[*][b]Localised menu[/b] — English and 简体中文 out of the box, and the menu follows the game's own language.
   Menu wording can be overridden from a plain-text file, no rebuild needed.
[/list]

[b][size=4]How it works (short version)[/size][/b]

Elden Ring's Spirit Ash system already knows how to spawn a PlayerIns-based body and hand it to the AI. ER Echo
rewrites a few BuddyParam rows at runtime so a chosen Ash spawns that body, then injects the exported profile
(face bytes, ChrAsm equipment, PlayerGameData stats) into the clone. Because the clone is a real player-type
entity, the game renders and animates it exactly like your character. Nothing is written to regulation.bin or
your .sl2.

[b][size=4]Requirements[/size][/b]

[list]
[*][b]A working vanilla install.[/b] Before adding any mod, confirm the game reaches the title screen and
   stays up for a minute [b]without[/b] Mod Engine 2. If it crashes without mods, this mod will not fix it —
   verify the game files / reinstall first.
[*][b]ELDEN RING 1.17.2[/b] (Steam, PC). eldenring.exe product version [b]2.7.2.0[/b] (worldwide) or
   [b]2.7.2.1[/b] (JP). [b]This is not optional[/b] — the mod resolves engine offsets and byte patterns for this
   exact build and will not work on other versions.
[*][b]A mod loader: Mod Engine 2 or me3.[/b] ME2 is what this was developed against (tested with 2.1.0);
   me3 works too, standalone for vanilla or bundled with The Convergence 3.x. Any loader that injects
   er_echo.dll into eldenring.exe with EAC disabled should work. The installer does not bundle a loader -
   it links you to the official pages.
[*][b]Windows 10/11 x64.[/b] No VC++ redistributable, no .NET, no Python required for the core mod.
[*][b]Offline mode.[/b] Launch through a mod loader, never through Steam's Play button (that starts EAC).
[*][b]Python 3.9+[/b] [i]optional[/i] — only for exporting profiles from a save and for the LLM sidecar.
[/list]

[b][size=4]Installation[/size][/b]

[b]Recommended: one-click installer[/b]

1. Back up %APPDATA%\EldenRing\<your SteamID>\ER0000.sl2.
2. Install a loader. For a vanilla install that is [b]Mod Engine 2[/b] in the game folder
   (...\ELDEN RING\Game); vanilla + me3 and Convergence + me3 also work. Don't have one? The installer
   links to the official Mod Engine 2 / me3 pages and lists the steps; no loader files are bundled.
3. Download the main file ([b]ER-Echo-Setup-0.1.0.zip[/b]), extract it anywhere and run
   [b]ER-Echo-Setup.exe[/b].
4. Set the game path — ...\ELDEN RING\Game for vanilla, or
   ...\Convergence3\ConvergenceER for Convergence/me3 — pick the loader (Auto / Mod Engine 2 / me3) and
   click [b]Install[/b]. The installer:
   [list]
   [*]copies [b]mods\ER-Echo\[/b] (DLL, generated er_echo.ini, talk ESD, tools, docs) and its own
       [b]config-er-echo.toml[/b]; it adds the er-echo entries to your config_eldenring.toml after a
       .bak backup - it never replaces the file. For me3 it appends to the .me3 profile instead,
   [*]exports your character(s) and writes [b]profiles=[/b] in er_echo.ini (the built-in Sanvenir stays at
       the end of the list),
   [*]backs up the config files it edits (`.bak-er-echo-*`) and has [b]Uninstall[/b] in the same window.
   [/list]
5. Click [b]Launch game[/b] in the same window (the finished-install dialog also offers to start the game).
   Vanilla runs [b]mods\ER-Echo\launch-er-echo.bat[/b], which passes -p .\eldenring.exe and so works around
   a Mod Engine 2 2.1.0 launcher crash; Convergence runs its own me3 with the right profile.

[b]Manual install[/b]: use the optional [b]ER Echo - Manual Install[/b] archive instead; unzip it into
the game folder and follow its README.txt (add external_dlls + mod_loader mods entry yourself).

If anything goes wrong, run the bundled self-check first (the path depends on how you installed):

[code]
# installer layout
powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File mods\ER-Echo\tools\doctor.ps1 -Target "C:\...\ELDEN RING\Game"
# manual layout
powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File er-echo\tools\doctor.ps1 -Target "C:\...\ELDEN RING\Game"
[/code]

It checks the game version, your ME2 config, the DLL's dependencies, your profile files, write permissions and
the mod's own language setting, and tells you what is missing.

[b][size=4]If the game does not start[/size][/b]

Three different failures look similar. Match the symptom before changing anything:

[b]1. The console window flashes and disappears.[/b] Event Viewer → Windows Logs → Application shows
[b]modengine2_launcher.exe[/b], exception [b]0xC0000409[/b], faulting module [b]ucrtbase.dll[/b].
Cause: Mod Engine 2 2.1.0's "-t er" auto-detects the Steam install path and aborts with an unhandled exception
on some machines. The bundled launcher passes -p .\eldenring.exe, which skips that detection. If you use your
own .bat, add -p ".\eldenring.exe".

[b]2. The game window appears, then closes after ~10 seconds.[/b] WER shows [b]eldenring.exe[/b],
[b]0xc0000005[/b], fault offset [b]0x1EBCEF9[/b]; the crash dump contains
"DLUserInputManagerImpl_win32.cpp(98)". Cause: Steam's in-game overlay (gameoverlayrenderer64.dll) collides
with Mod Engine 2's hooks in the game's input manager. Fix: run [b]launchmod_eldenring_admin.bat[/b] (manual
install) or tick [b]Launch as administrator[/b] / run [b]launch-er-echo-admin.bat[/b] with the installer — an
elevated process cannot have the overlay injected into it — or turn off Steam → Settings → In Game →
"Enable the Steam Overlay". Cost of the elevated launcher: no Steam overlay/friends panel in game.

[b]3. It crashes even with no mods loaded.[/b] The dump contains neither modengine2.dll nor er_echo.dll. This is
not the mod: verify the game files, repair Easy Anti-Cheat, or reinstall the game. Confirm the vanilla game
starts before adding mods back.

These are documented with reproduction steps in er-echo\docs\INSTALL.md §3 (and §3 of the English version).
When reporting a crash, attach the last ~50 lines of er_echo.log and the WER entry (module + offset).

[b][size=4]Exporting a character[/size][/b]

The installer does this for you on the Setup tab. The command line (manual install layout shown;
under the installer the tools live in [b]mods\ER-Echo\tools\[/b]):

[code]
python er-echo\tools\export_profile_from_save.py --list
python er-echo\tools\export_profile_from_save.py --slot 2 -o profiles\slot2.json
[/code]

Then in er_echo.ini:

[code]
[clone]
profiles=profiles/slot2.json,profiles/builtin_sanvenir.json
[/code]

Comma-separate several profiles to bring several characters (profiles=a.json,b.json). The built-in
[b]builtin_sanvenir.json[/b] is always appended by the installer; drop it from the list if you don't want it.
You can also export the character you are currently playing from inside the game (ipc_client.py dump_profile),
or a character from an old, backed-up save folder.

[b][size=4]Using it[/size][/b]

[list]
[*]Sit at a Site of Grace → the first entry is [b]Comrades (n/m)[/b] → party size, slot 1–3,
   [b]Companion AI[/b] (per-slot style), resummon, friendly fire, back.
[*]Summon with any Spirit Ash you have (the mod rewrites the Lone Wolf Ashes rows by default — configure
   buddy_rows for other ashes), or press [b]F8[/b] to summon directly.
[*][b]F6[/b] status, [b]F7[/b] dismiss, [b]F9[/b] reload profile, [b]F11[/b] toggle injection, [b]F12[/b] give
   the selected item to your companion (nothing selected = restore their profile loadout).
[*]Log: er_echo.log in the game folder. If something is wrong, that file is the first thing to read.
[/list]

[b][size=4]Optional: LLM battle director[/size][/b]

[code]
python er-echo\bridge\director.py --llm mock
python er-echo\bridge\director.py --llm openai --model gpt-4o-mini --api-key %OPENAI_API_KEY%
[/code]

mock runs fully offline and just applies a fixed policy. openai / ollama send combat state to the endpoint
[i]you[/i] choose — nothing is sent anywhere by the mod itself. The DLL only listens on 127.0.0.1:7811 for
local tools; it makes no outbound connections. This feature is optional and can be ignored entirely.

[b][size=4]Localisation[/size][/b]

Menu text follows the game: er_echo.ini → i18n section, language=[b]game[/b] (default), or pinned to
[b]en[/b] / [b]zh-CN[/b]. English and Simplified Chinese are bundled. Menu strings can also be overridden from a
plain-text file (er_echo_i18n.example.ini → er_echo_i18n.ini), so wording can be changed without a recompile.
See er-echo/docs/i18n.md.

[spoiler][b]简体中文说明[/b]

这个 mod 把「骨灰」变成你自己另一个存档里的角色：外观、体型、装备、等级、法术全部一致，战斗用游戏原生 AI。
支持一次召 1-3 个、赐福菜单里切换人数和号位、每个号位单独的「队友 AI」、玩家升级时队友跟着升级（并写回
profile）、队友伤害修正与玩家褪色者一致、敌人生命按出场人数补正、菜单开关友伤
（队友不会被当成敌人、也不会被锁定）、F12 把选中的装备给队友（没选中则把队友装备/法术恢复成档案原样），
以及可选的 LLM 战斗导演。随包带一个内置角色 **Sanvenir**（Lv1，彩蛋 / 备用），不导出也能直接玩。

安装（推荐，一键）：

1. 备份 `%APPDATA%\EldenRing\<你的 SteamID>\ER0000.sl2`；
2. 装好加载器：原版 + Mod Engine 2，或原版 / Convergence 3.x + me3（安装器里有官方下载链接和步骤说明，
   不打包、不分发加载器本身）；
3. 解压主文件 `ER-Echo-Setup-0.1.0.zip`，运行 `ER-Echo-Setup.exe`；
4. 填游戏路径（原版 `...\ELDEN RING\Game`；Convergence 为 `...\Convergence3\ConvergenceER`），
   选加载器（自动 / Mod Engine 2 / me3），点「一键安装」——它会拷文件、导出存档角色、写 `profiles=`、
   改加载器配置（都带备份），卸载也在同一页；
5. 点同一页的「启动游戏」。

手动安装：用可选的「Manual Install」压缩包，解到 `ELDEN RING\Game`，按包内 `README.txt` 自己加
`external_dlls` 和 `mod_loader` 条目，用包里带的 `launchmod_eldenring.bat` 启动（必须离线、关 EAC）。

导出自己的角色（可选；不导出就用内置的 Sanvenir）：

[code]
python er-echo\tools\export_profile_from_save.py --slot 2 -o profiles\slot2.json
[/code]

（安装器布局下工具在 `mods\ER-Echo\tools\`；也可以直接用安装器的「导出档案」页。）
然后 `er_echo.ini` 里 `profiles=profiles/slot2.json`（可逗号分隔多个；末尾保留
`profiles/builtin_sanvenir.json` 就还能带内置角色）。菜单语言默认在 i18n 段写 `language=game`
（跟随游戏文本语言），也可以固定成 `en` / `zh-CN`，安装器「游戏内菜单语言」下拉框会直接写入。

启动用包里的 `launchmod_eldenring.bat`（它带了 `-p`，绕开 ME2 2.1.0 启动器在某些机器上的 0xC0000409 崩溃）。
如果游戏窗口出现约 10 秒后闪退（WER：eldenring.exe / 0xc0000005 / 0x1EBCEF9），改用
`launchmod_eldenring_admin.bat`，或在 Steam → 设置 → 游戏中 关掉「启用 Steam 界面」。
装 mod 之前先确认「不带 mod 能正常进标题」。

出问题先看游戏根目录的 `er_echo.log`，或跑 `mods\ER-Echo\tools\doctor.ps1`（手动包：`er-echo\tools\doctor.ps1`）自检。[/spoiler]

[b][size=4]Known limitations[/size][/b]

[list]
[*][b]Version-locked.[/b] A game update breaks the mod until the offsets and patterns are re-mapped and it is
   rebuilt. Do not report "not working" on a different version without checking er_echo.log.
[*][b]Offline only.[/b] Not usable, and not safe, online.
[*][b]Mod conflicts.[/b] Other mods that rewrite the same parameter rows (BuddyParam, NpcParam,
   NpcThinkParam, BuddyStoneParam) or the same talk/ESD content can fight with it. Rule of thumb: test with
   only this mod first, then add others back one at a time.
[*][b]Spirit Ash choice.[/b] Out of the box it rewrites the Lone Wolf Ashes rows. Other ashes work too, but you
   have to map their rows in er_echo.ini (buddy_rows) — see docs/usage.md.
[*][b]Beta.[/b] The core loop is tested end-to-end on 1.17.2, but this is a 0.x release. Keep a clean save
   and a backup.
[*][b]Optional ESD fallback.[/b] Only for the rare case where the runtime-injected entry never appears. The
   separate archive carries a patched talk ESD and `switch_menu_mode.ps1`, which copies it into the folder your
   loader actually mounts (`mods\ER-Echo\mod\` with the installer, `<Game>\mod\` with the manual archive) and
   sets `nested_menu=false`. It conflicts with any other mod that edits the same file - merge, don't overwrite.
[*][b]Launcher depends on your environment.[/b] The bundled launchers already carry the -p workaround. The
   10-second crash is environment-specific (Steam overlay + ME2 hooks); on most machines the normal launcher
   works, on some the admin one is required.
[/list]

[b][size=4]FAQ[/size][/b]

[b]Is this a save editor?[/b] No. Characters are read from a copy of your save for export; nothing is written to
any .sl2.

[b]Can I use it with Seamless Co-op / other overhaul mods?[/b] Not recommended online, and large overhauls change
the same params. Offline, with only this mod plus cosmetic mods, it is the tested configuration.

[b]The grace menu has no "Comrades" entry.[/b] Check er_echo.log for ezstate: lines. The entry is injected at
runtime; if injection failed you can still summon with F8. Report the log lines.

[b]The clone looks like me, not like my other character.[/b] That means no profile was loaded — check the
profiles= path and run doctor.ps1.

[b]Does it work with the DLC?[/b] Yes, tested with Shadow of the Erdtree installed. The DLC itself is not required.

[b]The game exits about 10 seconds after launching.[/b] Steam overlay vs ME2 hooks. Use
launchmod_eldenring_admin.bat, or disable the Steam in-game overlay. See the troubleshooting section above.

[b]The launcher window closes immediately and the game never starts.[/b] ME2's Steam path auto-detection
aborted. Make sure the .bat passes -p ".\eldenring.exe" (the bundled one does).

[b]Do I lose anything by using the admin launcher?[/b] The Steam overlay (friends, browser, overlay
screenshots) is not injected into an elevated process. Steam achievements and cloud saves were not re-tested
in elevated mode — verify on a throwaway save if that matters to you.

